  "limitations": [
    "This reader is a declaration validator, not a certificate that the entire Type1 program conforms. It is not used by the native decoder.",
    "Executable clear-text preambles and other dictionary statements are not validated for all effects. Merely tracking lexical groups and dictionary depth does not establish their semantics.",
    "Encrypted private data, synthetic/hybrid font behavior and mutations outside the clear-text declaration are not validated.",
    "Raw names still require a validated CharStrings lookup and existing Adobe-name conversion before any Unicode can be emitted. MissingGlyph is retained as a raw declaration; it is not emitted as text.",
    "File-size checks in the diagnostic runner assume immutable retained fixtures. Production loading must use the bounded neutral parser and existing cumulative font budgets."
  ],
  "next_action": "Validate the remaining clear-text statement and encrypted-program boundaries, or use a strict reader that reports those unsupported forms. Only after that certificate exists should the declaration reader be wired into simple-font fallback with precedence, identity and aggregate resource-limit tests.",
